.TH BINGUX-EFFECTS 1 "2026-10-28" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-effects \- sound effects engine for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-effects run
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects restore
.br
.B bingux-effects render
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects presets
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects scan
.br
.B bingux-effects import
.I FILE
.RB { output | input }
.RI [ NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-effects
puts a chain of audio plugins between applications and the speakers
.RB ( output )
or between a microphone and applications
.RB ( input ).
It turns the active preset into a PipeWire
.B filter-chain
configuration and runs it as its own PipeWire client, one process for each
direction.
It creates a virtual device (\(lqEffects (Output)\(rq or \(lqEffects (Input)\(rq),
makes it the default device and sends the result to the real device.
When it stops, the real device is the default again.
.PP
Bingux Settings, under Sound, Effects, edits the presets and turns the effects
on and off.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "run " DIRECTION
Run one direction until stopped. The user unit
.B bingux-effects@output.service
does this.
.TP
.B restore
Start each direction that Settings has turned on. Run it at login.
.TP
.BI "render " DIRECTION
Print the filter-chain configuration for the active preset.
.TP
.BI "presets " DIRECTION
List the presets.
.TP
.B scan
List the plugins found, as JSON.
.TP
.BI "import " "FILE DIRECTION " [ NAME ]
Read an EasyEffects, Equalizer APO or AutoEq preset and save it as a Bingux preset.
.SH PLUGINS
Plugins come from PipeWire's built-in filters (equaliser, gain, delay, convolver),
from
.B libbingux_dsp.so
(compressor, limiter, gate, reverb and others), and from any LADSPA library found
in
.BR LADSPA_PATH ,
.IR ~/.ladspa ,
.I /usr/lib/ladspa
and the other usual directories.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LADSPA_PATH
Where to look for LADSPA libraries, instead of the usual directories.
.TP
.B BINGUX_LADSPA_PATH
More directories to look in.
.TP
.B BINGUX_EFFECTS_BIN
The
.B bingux-effects
program that Settings starts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/effects/state.json
What is on, the preset and the device.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/effects/{output,input}/presets/NAME.json
One preset per file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bingux/effects/plugins.json
The plugin scan, cached by file date.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bingux/effects/
The generated configuration, process id and level meters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/audio-effects.md in the Bingux source.
.SH AUTHORS
Kieran Drewett and the Bingux contributors.
